Found by mcp-hub-worker during k138 (2026-11-06).
A start that a stop calls off is logged differently by the transports: Http's start_p catch logs it at debug ("start called off by a stop"), Stdio's start_p catch logs it at error ("handshake failed: upstream NAME: stopped") -- since k138 that start fails at once as stopped. A configuration reload that replaces a starting stdio entry thus writes an error line for something that is no failure.
Done when: Stdio logs a start a stop called off as Http does (debug, no "handshake failed"), while a start that fails on its own still logs at error; checked with a test that captures the log.

